src/vendor/plutosvg/ and src/vendor/plutovg/ are the files listed in
tools/plutosvg-files.txt and tools/plutovg-files.txt, copied from the
archives to the same relative paths, with exactly the patches above
applied. tools/verify-vendor re-derives both trees from the pinned archives
and the patch series and fails on any other difference. Every patch is
minimal and offered upstream; each is named in zusvg_info().

Left out: plutosvg-ft.h (compiled only under PLUTOSVG_HAS_FREETYPE), CMake,
Meson, the tests, the examples and the images. Compile configuration, in
src/Makevars, with the reason for each there: PLUTOVG_BUILD_STATIC and
PLUTOSVG_BUILD_STATIC (never the *_BUILD macros, which export the API past
$(C_VISIBILITY)); STBIDEF, STBIWDEF and STBTT_DEF set to extern (hidden);
PLUTOVG_DISABLE_FONT_FACE_CACHE_LOAD; STBI_NO_* for every image format but
PNG and JPEG; STBI_NO_THREAD_LOCALS; HAVE_THREADS_H and
PLUTOSVG_HAS_FREETYPE undefined. R's -DNDEBUG removes the vendored
assert()s in an installed build.

GitHub publishes no uploaded release asset for these tags, so each archive
is the one GitHub generates from the tag. Hash verification is
trust-on-first-use: the SHA-256s above were computed at import time and are
re-checked by tools/verify-vendor. If GitHub ever regenerates an archive
with different bytes, verification fails, and the new archive must be
compared against the recorded commit before the digest is updated.

